<title>JAPAN: Showa Aluminum shares up on firm earnings.</title>
<headline>Showa Aluminum shares up on firm earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Showa Aluminum Corp were higher on Thursday morning, reflecting strong earnings for the interim period announced the day before, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0141 GMT, the shares were 12 yen higher at 622 yen in turnover of 1.292 million shares.  </p>
<p>On Wednesday, the aluminium processor said that its parent current profit for the six months to September 30, 1996, was 3.37 billion yen versus 1.71 billion yen in the previous year.</p>
</text>
